{"person_id": "lawrence-roberts", "name": "Lawrence Roberts", "category": "Computer vision / ARPANET architect", "birth_year": 1937, "age_at_milestone": 25, "milestone_by_age_26": "Completed MIT PhD in 1963 at age 25 with thesis 'Machine Perception of Three-Dimensional Solids,' foundational to computer vision; BS 1959, MS 1960, PhD 1963 all at MIT EE.", "early_history_summary": "Born December 21, 1937 in Westport, Connecticut, to two PhD chemists. Early electronics tinkerer (homemade phone network, TV). MIT electrical engineering degrees through PhD (1963) on 3D machine perception; later Lincoln Lab networking experiments and ARPA program manager who designed/oversaw ARPANET implementation.", "primary_leverage_engine": "Scarce technical / intellectual depth", "normalized_primary_engine": "Scarce technical / intellectual depth", "secondary_engine": "Network / capital", "started_serious_reps_before_20_score": 1, "prior_reps_score": 2, "scarce_skill_depth_score": 3, "native_distribution_score": 0, "elite_ecosystem_network_score": 2, "complementary_team_score": 1, "structural_wave_score": 2, "concentration_intensity_score": 2, "capital_safety_score": 1, "domain_proximity_score": 1, "success_tier": 1, "leverage_evidence_confidence": "High", "family_context_summary": "Westport, Connecticut; both parents (Elliot and Elizabeth Roberts) were PhD chemists—unusually strong scientific household.", "parent_family_domain_summary": "Parents were research chemists with doctorates, providing scientific literacy and likely educational expectations, though not computer networking specifically.", "early_family_financial_platform_support_score": 1, "parent_family_domain_advantage_score": 1, "inherited_audience_business_network_score": 0, "elite_institution_performance_pipeline_score": 2, "frontier_geography_ecosystem_score": 1, "rare_early_tools_facilities_score": 1, "dedicated_mentor_coach_tutor_score": 1, "exceptional_peer_cofounder_sibling_score": 0, "early_online_platform_community_score": 0, "direct_customer_domain_exposure_score": 0, "prodigy_physical_edge_score": 1, "adversity_constraint_catalyst_score": 0, "primary_early_advantage_archetype": "Elite performance pipeline", "primary_early_advantage_tags": "MIT EE PhD track, chemist parents, early electronics tinkering, Lincoln Lab/ARPA path", "evidence_summary": "Roberts's 1963 MIT computer-vision PhD at 25 is a clear ≤26 material research milestone (often called father of computer vision). Dual-PhD chemist parents and MIT pipeline accelerated him; later ARPANET program management (from 1966, age 28-29) made him an Internet pioneer. Founded Telenet and later networking startups.", "early_advantage_evidence_confidence": "High", "source_count": 4, "primary_source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawrence_Roberts_(scientist)", "source_urls": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawrence_Roberts_(scientist)", "https://www.britannica.com/biography/Lawrence-Roberts", "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/30/obituaries/lawrence-g-roberts-dies-at-81.html", "https://computerhistory.org/profile/larry-roberts/"], "starting_point": "Born Westport, CT, 1937 to two PhD chemists; early electronics hobbyist; MIT EE through PhD (1963).", "current_position": "Died December 26, 2018 at age 81 in Redwood City, CA; final roles included serial networking entrepreneur after ARPA/Telenet career.", "current_position_year": 2018, "is_living": false, "trajectory": [{"year": 1959, "age": 21, "event": "Earned MIT B.S. in electrical engineering."}, {"year": 1963, "age": 25, "event": "Completed MIT PhD on machine perception of three-dimensional solids (foundational computer vision)."}, {"year": 1965, "age": 27, "event": "At Lincoln Lab, achieved ARPA-funded computer-to-computer connection experiment."}, {"year": 1966, "age": 28, "event": "Hired by ARPA to design and manage what became the ARPANET."}, {"year": 1969, "age": 31, "event": "ARPANET initial deployment under his program leadership."}, {"year": 1973, "age": 35, "event"